{
  "meta": {
    "artifact": "readiness-snapshots",
    "title": "LingoLinq Findings Snapshots",
    "description": "Append-only time series of findings-register states, used to derive risk movement (new / movedOutOfOpen / reopened / severityChanged) between generations. Every snapshot stores the full open-finding ID set so flow is derived from prior/current ID sets, never from mutable counters. Multiple snapshots per day are allowed; generatedAt (full ISO 8601 timestamp) is the unique identity. Prior snapshots must never be mutated or reordered. Snapshots are appended ONLY by `ruby scripts/readiness-check.rb --snapshot` - the one mode permitted to read the wall clock. Each record after the first pins its predecessor's exact bytes via priorSnapshotSha.",
    "owner": "Scot Wahlquist",
    "governance": "Historical snapshots are hash-chained and Git-reviewed for immutability, and additionally, in CI (`--check`), compared byte-for-byte against the PR's base branch: every snapshot record already committed on base must survive as an unchanged, same-order prefix; only appending new suffix records is permitted. The priorSnapshotSha chain is an internal-consistency control (catches a quiet one-record edit) - it is NOT the append-only enforcement boundary by itself, because a rewrite that regenerates flows and chain shas for the entire subsequent history is internally self-consistent. The base-branch comparison is what makes such a coordinated rewrite fail CI. Outside --check (no base ref available, e.g. local dev before fetching origin/staging), this degrades to a warning, never a silent claim of protection.",
    "schemaVersion": "0.1.0",
    "generatedDate": "2026-08-11"
  },
